{what}

## Where it is
{where}

## How to verify it's done
{verify}

## Constraints
{constraints}

## Code economy note
{economy}

## Branch name
`feature/world-time` (single stacked branch; one PR closes all four)

## Concept for learning materials
{concept}
"""

COMMON = ("Plan: .claude/plans/world-time-and-schedules.md. ONE clock: every "
          "consumer reads WorldState's world_time; nothing keeps a private "
          "timer. Sky, fog color, and light level derive from the same hour "
          "(fog must keep melting into the horizon at night). "
          "make -C tests test stays green.")

SPECS = [
    {"title": "feat(core): WorldState — shared fact store with the world clock",
     "what": ("Generic string-keyed fact store (WorldFact{number,text}) owned "
              "by World — the 'world bus' gossip/journal will reuse. First "
              "fact: world_time_seconds, advanced by World::update at 1 real "
              "second = 1 game minute, starting 09:00, wrapping 24h; typed "
              "convenience accessors read the same fact any system could."),
     "where": "NEW src/core/WorldState.{hpp,cpp}; src/core/World.{hpp,cpp}; tests/test_world_state.cpp.",
